    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54390" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταληπ-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to check</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ θορυβητικοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1380
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>conveying direct apprehension</i> of an object, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. φαντασία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Stoic.</u>
					2.26
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					2.120
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					4.22
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				<i>by direct apprehension,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Stoic.
					2.27
				</span></i>
			; <i>manifestly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίνεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cleom.
					1.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
